      "f_ir": {
        "name": "advantage_weighted_logsigmoid_pairwise_norm_scaled_tanh_diff_centered_shifted_v1",
        "intuition": "To fix novelty failure due to excessive similarity to prior candidates, I replaced the weighted mean centering of the log probability difference with a weighted median-like robust centering approach using a clipped weighted mean shift combined with an offset shift based on the advantage statistic. This changes the functional form significantly by integrating an advantage-weighted shift and introduces asymmetric bounding via clamping before normalization. The loss now computes diff_raw minus a shifted center combining weighted mean and advantage gap-based offset, then normalizes by the norm of (advantage_gap + epsilon) plus an extra smooth softplus scale. This modification breaks the near-identity with prior candidates by altering the centering and normalization mechanism and introducing an adaptive shift related to advantage signals while maintaining smooth gradients and the log-sigmoid link.",
        "pseudocode": "epsilon=1e-6\nlpw = batch['log_prob_w']\nlpl = batch['log_prob_l']\nweight = batch['weight']\nadv = batch['advantage_gap']\ndiff_raw = lpw - lpl\nweighted_diff_sum = sum(diff_raw * weight)\nweight_sum = sum(weight)\nmean_diff = weighted_diff_sum / max(weight_sum, epsilon)\nclamped_diff_shift = clamp(mean_diff + 0.1 * mean(adv * weight) / max(weight_sum, epsilon), -0.5, 0.5)\ndiff_centered = diff_raw - clamped_diff_shift\nnorm_adv = norm(adv + epsilon)\nnorm_value = max(norm_adv + softplus(0.1), epsilon)\nstable_diff = diff_centered / norm_value\nsmooth_diff = tanh(stable_diff)\nscaled_diff = scale * smooth_diff\nloss = -logsigmoid(scaled_diff)\nweighted_loss = loss * weight\nloss_sum = sum(weighted_loss)\ntotal_weight = sum(weight)\nreturn loss_sum / max(total_weight, epsilon)",
