        "intuition": "Fixed high similarity by introducing a sign-based adaptive margin offset that shifts the log_prob difference proportional to the sign of advantage_gap norm deviation from its mean, breaking symmetry and pattern similarity. Used a stable scalar margin offset calculated as mean norm plus a small scaled signed deviation. This avoids direct subtraction of margin from the scaled difference and incorporates minor directional information without looping or complex ops. The normalization uses norm of advantage_gap as before, but the margin is now a shifted scalar ensuring variation across batches. Weighting and stable clamping remain unchanged, preserving numerical stability and pairwise logic. These changes reduce similarity while maintaining correctness and efficiency with vectorized ops.",
